7. The learned counsel for the appellant submitted that the averments in the claim petition are false;
that the deceased, who was shown as the pillion rider, was the actual rider; that he was in an inebriated condition; and hence, the finding on negligence by the Tribunal has to be set aside.
8. The learned counsel for the 1st respondent/claimant, per contra, submitted that the award of the Tribunal is justified and there is no reason to interfere with the award.
